<title>FRANCE: MATIF March financial futures, options volume up.</title>
<headline>MATIF March financial futures, options volume up.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of financial futures and options contracts traded on the French MATIF exchange in March rose 27.9 percent from the previous month and rose 0.9 percent compared to March 1996, MATIF said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for financial contracts were as follows:</p>
<p>			   Volume     Change    Change  Open positions</p>
<p>					 on month   on year  at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	6.26 million  +27.9 pct    +0.9 pct   914,212</p>
<p>  Financial futures 5.26 million  +34.9 pct    +3.0 pct   469,455</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond 3.53 million  +42.5 pct    +6.9 pct   156,889</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR	 1.15 million  +18.6 pct    +0.2 pct   241,715</p>
<p>     -  CAC-40	     529,044  +26.9 pct    -9.6 pct    65,251</p>
<p>     -  Ecu bond	    47,627  +49.3 pct   -29.8 pct     5,600</p>
<p>  Financial options	997,586   +0.2 pct    -9.1 pct   444,757</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     -  French bond	838,548   +6.8 pct    +7.5 pct   236,334</p>
<p>     -  PIBOR		157,209  -23.9 pct   -47.6 pct   205,655</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
